// =============================================================================
// Sable Vey — Jeweler / Lapidary.  Questline: "Aether's Facet" (vendor.jeweler)
// Keystone: the First Heartgem.  Teaches gem sockets + rare spawns; moral choice.
// The Stage-3 branch sets $sableChoiceReported (feeds Coppin / late Necromancer reveal).
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToJeweler
---
<<if $q_jeweler_stage == 0>>
    Sable: Raw aether? Crude. Cut it right and it sings — and sings louder in the right hands.
    -> Show me what it can do.
        Sable: Bring me a flawless crystal. The kind that only surfaces when the veil's thin. Then I'll show you what aether can really do.
        <<set $q_jeweler_stage = 1>>
        <<StartQuest vendor.jeweler>>
        Sable: "Aether's Facet." Chase the rare spawn — and be quick, it fades.
    -> Just browse the gems.
        <<OpenShop "jeweler">>
<<elseif $q_jeweler_stage == 1>>
    Sable: Did you catch a flawless one before it faded?
    -> Here it is.
        <<AdvanceQuest vendor.jeweler>>
        <<set $q_jeweler_stage = 2>>
        Sable: <i>She holds it to the light.</i> Exquisite. Now — your first heartgem. Hold still while I cut and socket it. This is where aether stops being a resource and starts being power.
    -> Still chasing it.
        Sable: They surface when the veil thins. Patience, then speed.
<<elseif $q_jeweler_stage == 2>>
    Sable: Is the heartgem socketed and settled?
    -> It's set.
        <<AdvanceQuest vendor.jeweler>>
        <<set $q_jeweler_stage = 3>>
        Sable: <i>She lowers her voice.</i> Now — a confession. I've been selling cut aether to a broker outside Elarion. Coin's coin. I could cut your gems cheaper if you... look elsewhere. Or you tell the village, and earn their trust instead.
        -> Keep your secret. (cheaper gems)
            Sable: Sensible. Our little arrangement. Come back for discounted facets.
            <<AdvanceQuest vendor.jeweler>>
            <<GiveKeystone "FirstHeartgem">>
            <<set $q_jeweler_stage = 9>>
            Sable: The First Heartgem is yours. Discretion suits you.
        -> Report the broker. (village trust)
            Sable: <i>She stiffens, then nods.</i> ...You're right. I'll come clean. Better the village's trust than a stranger's coin.
            <<set $sableChoiceReported = true>>
            <<AdvanceQuest vendor.jeweler>>
            <<GiveKeystone "FirstHeartgem">>
            <<set $q_jeweler_stage = 9>>
            Sable: The First Heartgem is yours, honestly earned. Tell Coppin to watch his roads — that broker pays in dirty Glimmer.
    -> Not yet.
        Sable: A gem half-cut is just a rock. Finish it.
<<else>>
    Sable: The Heartgem-bearer. My finest work walks on your gear. What do you need cut?
    -> Browse gems.
        <<OpenShop "jeweler">>
    -> Upgrade the lapidary.
        <<OpenUpgrade "jeweler">>
    -> Nothing today.
        Sable: Mind who's buying, hm?
<<endif>>
===
